Changed [process.rs](/home/admin/src/filmcraft-wt/runner/crates/scenerender/src/process.rs), [ingest.rs](/home/admin/src/filmcraft-wt/runner/crates/scenerender/src/ingest.rs), [fake.rs](/home/admin/src/filmcraft-wt/runner/crates/scenerender/src/fake.rs), and [lib.rs](/home/admin/src/filmcraft-wt/runner/crates/scenerender/src/lib.rs:20). The only lib.rs change is the requested test-only fake-module declaration.

Public API (`Result` means `filmcraft_media::Result`):

```rust
pub struct RunOutput {
    pub code: Option<i32>,
    pub stdout_tail: String,
    pub stderr_tail: String,
}
pub trait Runner: Send + Sync {
    fn run(&self, program: &Path, args: &[OsString], cwd: &Path,
           timeout: Duration) -> Result<RunOutput>;
}
pub struct ProcessRunner; // implements Runner
pub fn check(out: &RunOutput) -> Result<()>;
pub fn read_frame(path: &Path, width: u32, height: u32,
                  max_bytes: u64) -> Result<VideoFrame>;
```

Test support:

```rust
pub enum Behaviour {
    Ok { width: u32, height: u32 },
    ExitInvalid, ExitIo, WrongSize, NoOutput, Hang, NoAudio,
}
impl FakeRenderer {
    pub fn new(behaviour: Behaviour) -> Self;
    pub fn program(&self) -> &Path;
    pub fn dir(&self) -> &Path;
    pub fn invocations(&self) -> Vec<String>;
}
```

Design notes:

- Independent guarded reader threads retain bounded 64 KiB tails, including after lossy UTF-8 conversion. Polling is every 15 ms; diagnostics retain at most 2 KiB.
- Timeout and cancellation kill and reap the direct child. Transient executable-busy errors retry within the same timeout and cancellation limits.
- PNG input is capped by `min(max_bytes, 256 MiB)`; RGBA8 output is capped at 256 MiB. Dimensions are validated before and after decoding. `VideoFrame::rgba8` supplies straight-alpha RGBA8 and `SRGB_FULL`.
- Process/filesystem implementations have wasm `Unsupported` fallbacks. No dependencies were added.
- Fake directories clean up on Drop. `WrongSize` emits 1×1; `NoAudio` renders 2×2 video. Probes succeed for every behaviour.

TDD log — all names below are under their module’s `tests` namespace:

| Tests | Observed red failure → green |
|---|---|
| process: `exit_codes_and_diagnostics`, `drains_megabytes_from_both_pipes_and_bounds_lossy_tails`, `signal_is_an_io_error`, `stdin_is_closed`, `fake_render_frames_are_ingested` | Unwrapped `Unsupported("scene-render process stub")` → passed |
| process: `diagnostic_tail_is_utf8_safe_and_bounded` | Unexpected `Unsupported("scene-render check stub")` → passed |
| process: `timeout_kills_and_reaps_promptly`, `cancellation_is_polled_on_the_caller_thread`, `missing_program_is_io` | Expected timeout-Io, Cancelled, and Io assertions failed → passed |
| ingest: `good_png_preserves_straight_alpha_and_srgb`, `sixteen_bit_png_becomes_eight_bit` | Unwrapped `Unsupported("scene-render ingest stub")` → passed |
| ingest: `wrong_size_is_rejected`, `corrupt_pngs_are_errors_not_panics`, `hostile_dimensions_are_rejected_without_allocating` | Expected Decode assertions failed → passed |
| ingest: `file_cap_is_checked_before_decode`, `missing_file_is_io` | Expected Io assertions failed → passed |
| fake: `probes_and_invocations`, `render_flags_are_named_and_range_is_exclusive`, `encode_writes_valid_wav` | `out.status.success()` failed → passed |
| fake: `failure_and_output_behaviours`, `no_audio_keeps_video_available` | Exit code `Some(99)` instead of `Some(1)` → passed |
| fake: `hang_is_killable_and_directories_are_unique_and_removed` | `still_running` assertion failed → passed |
| process: `busy_executable_is_retried_until_writer_closes` | `Io("scene-render spawn: Text file busy (os error 26)")` → passed |
| process: `busy_executable_respects_timeout`, `busy_executable_respects_cancellation` | Expected timeout-Io and Cancelled assertions failed → passed |

Initial red: 22 failures, one existing test passed. After fixing one compiler type-annotation error, all 23 passed. Adding bit-flip mutation coverage exposed an intermittent executable-busy failure; three deterministic regressions failed before the retry implementation and passed afterward.

Final VM results: `cargo clippy -p filmcraft-scenerender --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed; crate tests **26 passed, 0 failed**, doc-tests **0**; `cargo check -p filmcraft-scenerender --target wasm32-unknown-unknown` passed. All touched files were rustfmt-ed; `git diff --check` passed. No local builds or tests ran.

Integrator note: cleanup targets the direct child, not its process tree. If descendants retain output pipes, unfinished reader threads detach until EOF so they cannot block timeout handling. No edits outside scope are required.
